    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and both its tests pass along with a full `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field derived from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table.\n\nThe endpoint tested is `GET /api/owners/{id}`, which serializes an owner via `OwnerDto` (generated from `openapi.yml`) and `OwnerMapper`, which already computes derived read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `membershipTier`, \u2026) with MapStruct expressions. I followed that same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `locality` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../rest/function/common/Localities.java`** (new) \u2014 holds the fixed table (`Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD`) and a `region(city)` method returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any other city (including null).\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", ...)` expression that calls `Localities.region(owner.getCity())`.\n\nResult: `Sydney` \u2192 `NSW`, and an unknown city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`, matching both acceptance tests. Full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests).",
